## Why This Is Asked

Gauges practical, client-side prompt evaluation with safety and tone controls for high-stakes brands. Focuses on a beginner-friendly rubric and a concrete routing prototype, suitable for scalable chat systems.

## Key Concepts

- Prompt scoring rubrics
- Client-side routing logic
- Safety and bias considerations
- Minimal unit testing for NLP-ish logic

## Code Example

```javascript
function routePrompt(input){
  const lower = input.toLowerCase();
  const clarity = /order|status|refund/.test(lower) ? 4 : 2;
  const safety = !lower.includes('password') ? 4 : 2;
  const bias = /(racial|gender|biased)/.test(lower) ? 5 : 1;
  if (clarity >= 4 && safety >= 4 && bias <= 2) return 'concise';
  if (lower.includes('please') || lower.includes('sorry')) return 'empathetic';
  return 'authoritative';
}
```

